.TH CYCLO 1 "August 2026" "Cyclo 0.2.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cyclo \- run Git-defined agent teams through composable model providers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cyclo
.RI [ --state-root\  DIR ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cyclo
is a per-user host command for Git-defined agent teams.  It builds local
component images and delegates container lifecycle to DComp.  Cyclo requires a
local Docker Engine and a DComp executable with machine API version 1.
.PP
Cyclo does not run as a daemon. Its upstream default shared realm uses state
in
.I /var/lib/cyclo
and system configuration in
.IR /etc/cyclo/host.conf .
This package creates the state root world-readable and writable as a temporary
shared-state policy. Cyclo leaves ownership, modes, groups, and ACLs to the
host filesystem; use a trusted Unix group and ACLs for a secure multi-user
installation.
.PP
Do not run Cyclo as root.  The invoking user must have access to the local
Docker socket.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B team init
Create a team repository from a bundled template.
.TP
.B project init
Create a project definition with team and project mounts.
.TP
.B validate
Validate a team or project definition without starting a workload.
.TP
.B gateway
Inspect providers, log in, build the gateway, or destroy its credential store.
.TP
.B run, start, stop, ps, inspect, logs
Manage persisted project instances.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the host Docker and DComp prerequisites.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/cyclo
Default shared Cyclo state root. This package creates it with mode 0777;
Cyclo does not alter filesystem access policy at runtime.
.TP
.I /etc/cyclo/host.conf
Comment-only packaged provider-component configuration for the default shared
realm.
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed README at
.I /usr/share/doc/cyclo/README.md.gz
and the project documentation describe team, project, and provider formats.
.SH AUTHOR
Cyclo was written by Gianluca Guida.
